{"additions":210,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nThe Projects page refreshed the linked-project list on activation but never the board itself: once fetched, a board was served from `board_cache` for the rest of the session, silently going stale with no age indicator. This PR keeps a fetch time per board, re-fetches a stale board (> 5 min) on page activation and after a list refresh — the old board stays visible until the new one swaps in (`set_board()` keeps the selected card by id) — and shows the board's age in the status bar.\n\nCloses #140\n\n## Changes\n\n- `src/projects/state.rs`\n  - `board_cache` now maps to `CachedBoard { board, fetched_at: Option<Instant> }`; `fetched_at: None` means the fetch time is unknown and the board is always considered stale\n  - One named constant `STALE_AFTER` (5 min, formerly `LIST_REFRESH_AFTER`) governs both the list refresh and board staleness\n  - `sync_board()` fills the cache from disk with the file's age (`Instant::now().checked_sub(age)`) and `spawn_board()`s whenever the cached board is stale — covering both project cycling and the post-list-refresh path\n  - `on_activate` also re-fetches the selected project's board when stale (guarded by `board_inflight`, so no duplicate fetch)\n  - `last_list_refresh` is recorded on a successful `Repo` result only, so a failed list read no longer pushes the next retry 5 minutes out; `on_activate` skips a re-spawn while one is already loading\n  - `board_age()` formats the shown board's age via the existing `format_relative` helper (`board 12m ago`)\n- `src/projects/domain/disk_cache.rs` — `load_board` becomes `load_board_with_age`, deriving the board's age from the cache file's mtime (the last fetch wrote it); an unreadable mtime counts as infinitely old\n- `src/core/ui/status_bar.rs` — the Projects status bar shows `board 12m ago` next to the item/column counts\n- `docs/config.md` — refresh-timing note in the Projects page section\n- Tests: stale board re-fetched on activation while the old one stays shown, fresh board (< 5 min) not re-fetched, failed list/board fetches do not suppress the retry, age formatting (`board just now` / `board 12m ago` / no age when unknown), file-age helper\n\n## Not verified\n\n- Not exercised against a live GitHub Project board (unit tests drive the state machine through the bg-message channel); the real `gh` round-trip path is unchanged\n- The status-bar age indicator was not screenshot-verified in a terminal\n- No demo tape re-recorded: the visible key flow is unchanged (the only UI delta is the status-bar age text)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w\n","changedFiles":5,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-31T09:26:48Z","deletions":25,"headRefName":"fix/projects-board-staleness","labels":[],"number":144,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLeU7Hg","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThere is a confirmed logic issue in board-loading state handling under concurrent/in-flight board fetches, and the PR also misses required demo tape/GIF updates for a user-visible UI change.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nThis PR improves the Projects page’s freshness guarantees by tracking per-board fetch timestamps, re-fetching boards that have gone stale on page activation (and after list refresh), and surfacing the board’s age in the status bar.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Track board fetch time in-memory (`CachedBoard { fetched_at }`) and treat unknown times as stale.\n- Extend disk cache loading to derive board age from cache file mtime; re-fetch stale boards while keeping the old board visible until swap-in.\n- Show “board … ago” in the Projects status bar and document the refresh behavior.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| `src/projects/state.rs` | Adds stale/age tracking to board cache, refreshes stale boards on activation, and formats board age for the status bar. |\r\n| `src/projects/domain/disk_cache.rs` | Loads cached boards along with file-age derived from mtime; adds helper/test coverage for file age. |\r\n| `src/core/ui/status_bar.rs` | Renders the board age indicator in the Projects status bar. |\r\n| `docs/config.md` | Documents the refreshed behavior and the new status-bar age indicator. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 4/4 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 2\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T09:31:21Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"b7f11737aff939428ff9e67163e842147d6b4305"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLeZbPg","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T09:37:46Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"4916225dbda006f618d59429e0bc1eb0265bc11a"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLeZdTw","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T09:37:48Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"4916225dbda006f618d59429e0bc1eb0265bc11a"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLebcpg","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟢 Approval recommended\n\nThe core behavior change is well-covered by targeted tests and appears consistent with the stated issue/requirements, with only a minor documentation formatting fix suggested.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (1)\n\n**Previously missed (1)** — in code that hasn't changed since the last review.\n\n**docs/config.md:433**\n* The inline code span in the example breaks across a newline (`` `board 12m`` on one line and ``ago` `` on the next). Markdown code spans cannot contain newlines, so this may render incorrectly.\n```\nComing back to the page after 5 minutes away re-reads the linked projects\nand re-fetches the shown board — the old board stays visible until the new\none arrives, and the status bar shows the board's age (e.g. `board 12m\nago`). `r` refreshes everything immediately; there is no polling while the\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 5/5 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 0 new\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T09:40:08Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"4916225dbda006f618d59429e0bc1eb0265bc11a"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T09:47:01Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33379371792/job/99447970183","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-08-31T09:47:02Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T09:39:10Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33378620467/job/99445651147","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T09:37:53Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2